          "type": "PARALLEL"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Parse Contacts and Replacement Type Code"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772427605556"
          },
          "code": "PARSE_CONTACTS_AND_REPLACEMENT_TYPE_CODE",
          "id": "1772427639761",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772427639763_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI Recall Extraction Assistant acting as a Medical Device Recall Specialist.\nScan {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_EXACT_HEADER_ATTRIBUTES.$output}} to create following two attributes in JSON payload :\n\n1. ReplacementTypeCode\n2. externalRecallContacts\n\nOutput MUST be a single valid RFC8259-compliant JSON object with ONLY these fields if they are present. \nIf neither field is produced, output {}.\n\nGENERAL RULES\n- Stateless: Use ONLY {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_EXACT_HEADER_ATTRIBUTES.$output}}.\n- Do NOT refer to, reuse, or assume anything from previous messages or recalls.\n- Do NOT include empty strings, empty arrays, or empty objects.\n- Escape string values according to RFC8259:\n  \" → \\\"\n  \\ → \\\\\n  \\n → \\\\n\n  \\t → \\\\t\n  \\r → \\\\r\n\n- Final output must be ONLY one JSON object — no commentary.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n1) REPLACEMENTTYPECODE (derived ONLY from action field)\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nScan the **action** field from {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_EXACT_HEADER_ATTRIBUTES.$output}}. Apply highest matching priority:\n\nPriority 1 — ORA_RETURN_WITH_CREDIT  \nTrigger if action contains any instruction to:\nreturn, ship back, send back, transfer, yield, hand over, obtain return authorization, obtain RMA, recover and return, arrange return.\n\nPriority 2 — ORA_SCH_CREDIT_ONLY  \nTrigger ONLY if:\n- No return action appears, AND\n- Action instructs: destroy, discard, dispose, eliminate, waste, scrap (on site).\n\nPriority 3 — ORA_CORRECTION  \nTrigger ONLY if:\n- No return action AND no destroy/dispose action, AND\n- Action includes: install, inspect, test, repair, upgrade, correct, label, investigate, remove, modify, replace, authorize repair, authorize correction, schedule correction, schedule service.\n\nIf none of the above appear, omit ReplacementTypeCode entirely.\n\nIf both return AND destroy appear → choose ORA_RETURN_WITH_CREDIT.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) EXTERNAL RECALL CONTACTS (externalRecallContacts)\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nBuild array externalRecallContacts from **action** and **additional_info_contact** in {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_EXACT_HEADER_ATTRIBUTES.$output}}.\n\nEach object may contain:\n- ContactName (required per object)\n- Telephone (optional)\n- Email (optional)\n\nExtraction rules:\n- ContactName: any person name OR department/business name found in action or additional_info_contact.\n- Telephone: match regex:\n  ^(\\+?[\\d]{1,3}[-.\\s]?)?(\\(0\\))?[\\d]{1,4}[-.\\s]?[\\d]{2,4}[-.\\s]?[\\d]{2,4}[-.\\s]?[\\d]{1,4}(\\s?(?i)Ext\\.?\\s?\\d+)?$\n- Email: must contain \"@\" and follow valid email-like pattern.\n- Fallback rule: If neither action nor additional_info_contact contains a valid contact name, add one object with ContactName = recalling_firm (if present). Include Telephone/Email only if available.\n- Omit Telephone or Email fields from an object if not available.\n- Only include externalRecallContacts if at least one valid contact object is produced.\n- Place externalRecallContacts under a list, for example:\n    \"externalRecallContacts\": [ ... ]\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT FORMAT\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nReturn only one JSON object, containing ONLY:\n\n{\n  \"ReplacementTypeCode\": \"...\",\n  \"externalRecallContacts\": [ ... ]\n}\n\nIf a field is not produced, omit it.\n\nIf both fields are omitted, return: {}\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Parse Dates from Code Info"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772427605556"
          },
          "code": "PARSE_DATES_FROM_CODE_INFO",
          "id": "1772427656911",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772427656912_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI Recall Extraction Assistant acting as a Medical Device Recall Specialist.\nScan {{$context.$nodes.GET_CODE_INFO.$output}} to create following two attributes in JSON payload :\n\n1. TrackStartDate | TrackStartDateProp | TrackStartDateSugg \n2. TrackEndDate | TrackEndDateProp | TrackEndDateSugg\n\nOutput MUST be a single valid RFC8259-compliant JSON object with ONLY these fields if they are present. \nIf neither field is produced, output {}.\n\nGENERAL RULES\n- Stateless: Use ONLY {{$context.$nodes.GET_CODE_INFO.$output}}.\n- Do NOT refer to, reuse, or assume anything from previous messages or recalls.\n- Do NOT include empty strings, empty arrays, or empty objects.\n- Escape string values according to RFC8259:\n  \" → \\\"\n  \\ → \\\\\n  \\n → \\\\n\n  \\t → \\\\t\n  \\r → \\\\r\n\n- Final output must be ONLY one JSON object — no commentary.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n1) TrackStartDate | TrackStartDateProp | TrackStartDateSugg (STRICTLY CONTROLLED) (derived ONLY from code_info field)\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nScan the **code_info** field from {{$context.$nodes.GET_CODE_INFO.$output}}. Apply highest matching priority:\n\n- Never use any field other than code_info.\n- Forbidden: Do NOT extract from any other fields.\n- Search only code_info (if present): code_info.\n- Extract a single start date if there is an explicit distribution start date.\n- If no distribution start date but a manufacturing start date is present (and context is manufacturer recall), use that manufacturing start date.\n- If only month and year are given (e.g., “Distributed from November 2000…”), output the first day of that month (e.g., 2000-11-01).\n- Output format: yyyy-MM-dd.\n- If you include any TrackStartDate* field, also include TrackStartDateSource with value \"code_info\". If you do not output a TrackStartDate* field, omit TrackStartDateSource.\n- If code_info does not contain a valid start date, omit all TrackStartDate* fields entirely.\n\nPositive examples:\n- Input: { \"code_info\": \"Distribution began on 2023-10-05.\" }\n  Output (subset): { \"TrackStartDateProp\":\"2023-10-05\",\"TrackStartDate\":\"2023-10-05\",\"TrackStartDateSugg\":\"2023-10-05\",\"TrackStartDateSource\":\"code_info\" }\n\n- Input: { \"code_info\": \"Manufacturing commenced on 2021-08-15 and product was immediately distributed.\" }\n  Output (subset): { \"TrackStartDateProp\":\"2021-08-15\",\"TrackStartDate\":\"2021-08-15\",\"TrackStartDateSugg\":\"2021-08-15\",\"TrackStartDateSource\":\"code_info\" }\n\nNegative examples:\n- Input: { \"code_info\":\"Recall initiated.\", \"event_date_initiated\":\"2021-05-20\" }\n  Output: {}\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) TrackEndDate | TrackEndDateProp | TrackEndDateSugg\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n- Attempt extraction only if code_info is present.\n- Scan the **code_info** field from {{$context.$nodes.GET_CODE_INFO.$output}}. Apply highest matching priority\n- Extract ONLY if an explicit date range is present in code_info, e.g.:\n  “distributed from [START] through [END]”\n  “shipments from [START] to [END]”\n  “between [START] and [END]”\n- END may be a full date or only month and year.\n- If only month and year for END (e.g., “May 2011”), output last day of that month as yyyy-MM-dd (e.g., 2011-05-31).\n- If only a single date is provided (no range), do not extract.\n- Omit if no valid end date is found.\n\nExamples (extract):\n- Input: { \"code_info\":\"All codes distributed from February 2008 through May 2011\" }\n  Output (subset): { \"TrackEndDateProp\":\"2011-05-31\" }\n\n- Input: { \"code_info\":\"Distribution occurred from Nov 2000 through April 2003.\" }\n  Output (subset): { \"TrackEndDateProp\":\"2003-04-30\" }\n\nExample (omit):\n- Input: { \"code_info\":\"Distribution began in February 2008.\" }\n  Output: {}\n\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT FORMAT\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nReturn only one JSON object, containing ONLY:\n\n{\n \"TrackStartDate\": \"...\",\n\"TrackEndDate\": \"...\",\n\"TrackStartDateSugg\": \"...\",\n\"TrackEndDateSugg\": \"...\",\n\"TrackStartDateProp\": \"...\",\n\"TrackEndDateProp\": \"...\"\n}\n\nIf a field is not produced, omit it.\n\nIf both fields are omitted, return: {}\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Parse Dates From Product Desc"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772427605556"
          },
          "code": "PARSE_DATES_FROM_PRODUCT_DESC",
          "id": "1772427674661",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772427674662_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI Recall Extraction Assistant acting as a Medical Device Recall Specialist.\nScan {{$context.$nodes.GET_PRODUCT_DESCRIPTION.$output}} to create following two attributes in JSON payload :\n\n1. TrackStartDate | TrackStartDateProp | TrackStartDateSugg \n2. TrackEndDate | TrackEndDateProp | TrackEndDateSugg\n\nOutput MUST be a single valid RFC8259-compliant JSON object with ONLY these fields if they are present. \nIf neither field is produced, output {}.\n\nGENERAL RULES\n- Stateless: Use ONLY {{$context.$nodes.GET_PRODUCT_DESCRIPTION.$output}}.\n- Do NOT refer to, reuse, or assume anything from previous messages or recalls.\n- Do NOT include empty strings, empty arrays, or empty objects.\n- Escape string values according to RFC8259:\n  \" → \\\"\n  \\ → \\\\\n  \\n → \\\\n\n  \\t → \\\\t\n  \\r → \\\\r\n\n- Final output must be ONLY one JSON object — no commentary.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n1) TrackStartDate | TrackStartDateProp | TrackStartDateSugg (STRICTLY CONTROLLED) (derived ONLY from product_description field)\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nScan the ** product_description** field from {{$context.$nodes.GET_PRODUCT_DESCRIPTION.$output}} . Apply highest matching priority:\n\n- Never use any field other than product_description.\n- Forbidden: Do NOT extract from any other fields.\n- Search only product_description (if present): product_description.\n- Extract a single start date if there is an explicit distribution start date.\n- If no distribution start date but a manufacturing start date is present (and context is manufacturer recall), use that manufacturing start date.\n- If only month and year are given (e.g., “Distributed from November 2000…”), output the first day of that month (e.g., 2000-11-01).\n- Output format: yyyy-MM-dd.\n- If you include any TrackStartDate* field, also include TrackStartDateSource with value \"product_description\". If you do not output a TrackStartDate* field, omit TrackStartDateSource.\n- If product_description does not contain a valid start date, omit all TrackStartDate* fields entirely.\n\nPositive examples:\n- Input: { \"product_description\": \"Distribution began on 2023-10-05.\" }\n  Output (subset): { \"TrackStartDateProp\":\"2023-10-05\",\"TrackStartDate\":\"2023-10-05\",\"TrackStartDateSugg\":\"2023-10-05\",\"TrackStartDateSource\":\"product_description\" }\n\n- Input: { \"product_description\": \"Manufacturing commenced on 2021-08-15 and product was immediately distributed.\" }\n  Output (subset): { \"TrackStartDateProp\":\"2021-08-15\",\"TrackStartDate\":\"2021-08-15\",\"TrackStartDateSugg\":\"2021-08-15\",\"TrackStartDateSource\":\"product_description\" }\n\nNegative examples:\n- Input: { \"product_description\":\"Recall initiated.\", \"event_date_initiated\":\"2021-05-20\" }\n  Output: {}\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) TrackEndDate | TrackEndDateProp | TrackEndDateSugg\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n- Attempt extraction only if product_description is present.\n- Scan the ** product_description** field from {{$context.$nodes.GET_PRODUCT_DESCRIPTION.$output}} . Apply highest matching priority\n- Extract ONLY if an explicit date range is present in product_description, e.g.:\n  “distributed from [START] through [END]”\n  “shipments from [START] to [END]”\n  “between [START] and [END]”\n- END may be a full date or only month and year.\n- If only month and year for END (e.g., “May 2011”), output last day of that month as yyyy-MM-dd (e.g., 2011-05-31).\n- If only a single date is provided (no range), do not extract.\n- Omit if no valid end date is found.\n\nExamples (extract):\n- Input: { \"product_description\":\"All codes distributed from February 2008 through May 2011\" }\n  Output (subset): { \"TrackEndDateProp\":\"2011-05-31\" }\n\n- Input: { \"product_description\":\"Distribution occurred from Nov 2000 through April 2003.\" }\n  Output (subset): { \"TrackEndDateProp\":\"2003-04-30\" }\n\nExample (omit):\n- Input: { \"product_description\":\"Distribution began in February 2008.\" }\n  Output: {}\n\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT FORMAT\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nReturn only one JSON object, containing ONLY:\n\n{\n \"TrackStartDate\": \"...\",\n\"TrackEndDate\": \"...\",\n\"TrackStartDateSugg\": \"...\",\n\"TrackEndDateSugg\": \"...\",\n\"TrackStartDateProp\": \"...\",\n\"TrackEndDateProp\": \"...\"\n}\n\nIf a field is not produced, omit it.\n\nIf both fields are omitted, return: {}\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
